  "description": "meme-id: camel_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts three camels with their mouths open, seemingly shouting or roaring, against a backdrop of a blue sky with clouds. The text overlay reads \"trust me...\" at the top and \"...they're re all terrorists\" at the bottom. The meme uses the visual of camels, which are often associated with the Middle East, to make a hateful and inflammatory statement by equating all members of a region or group (implied to be Middle Eastern or Muslim) with terrorism. This is a clear example of Islamophobia, as it directly links a broad group of people with terrorism, which is a harmful and hateful stereotype. The intent is to provoke, spread fear, and reinforce negative stereotypes about Muslims or people from the Middle East, making it a hateful meme.",
